    <!-- Màn hình: About -->
    <system:String x:Key="About_ApplicationInformation">Application information</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_HowItWorks">How it works</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ActivityLog">Activity log</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_VersionLabel">Version 1.0.3 ( Test )</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_Author">Author</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_SoftwareRepositoryManagerSRM">Software Repository Manager (SRM) is not really a project but a personal product made FOR FUN, born from the need to manage installers with the requirement of being simple, lightweight and, above all, able to run standalone and portable on external devices such as USB drives and external hard drives without much modification.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_About70OfThe">About 70% of the code was generated by AI; my own role is mostly direction, prompting features, fixing issues related to structure and variable names, fixing errors involving large amounts of text that the AI cannot read in a single session, testing, packaging and publishing publicly, so the source code is shared with anyone who wants to modify it or develop their own version based on this framework — of course, you are required to credit the original version name :) .</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_100OfTheCode">100% of the code is C# on the Visual Studio platform, combined with Blend for editing the interface, using the SQLite database engine — extremely compact and simple, with the principle of being as light as possible and as simple as possible while still being fully featured.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_TheMainFeaturesCurrently">the main features currently available in this version include: installer management | resource management | single / batch / set-based installation | installers with multiple attached versions and attached resources | a basic uninstaller that can tell system software from personal software | an automatic update scanning system with 120 pre-listed and flagged apps | 5 built-in basic tools.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_SinceThisIsPersonal">since this is personal software developed in spare time, bugs may slip through testing unnoticed, so if you find a bug, please contact me via Facebook using the button below.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ContactViaFacebook">Contact via Facebook</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ArchitectureSpecificationHow">Architecture Specification &amp; How It Works</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_1DatabaseArchitectureState">1. Database Architecture &amp; State Management</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_TheStorageSystemIs" xml:space="preserve">The storage system is designed to be fully decentralized (Serverless) through the SQLite engine. The </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ClassWillAutomaticallyComput" xml:space="preserve"> class will automatically compute the root folder (</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ToGenerateTheFile" xml:space="preserve">) to generate the file </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ThisGuaranteesAbsolute" xml:space="preserve">. This guarantees absolute </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_BehaviorWhenTheApp" xml:space="preserve"> behavior when the app runs from a USB drive. The integrity of the multi-dimensional data structure (such as Software, Versions, Presets) is tightly enforced through the foreign key mechanism </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_CombinedWith" xml:space="preserve"> combined with </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_WhenAParentSoftware">. When a parent software is removed, the Database automatically cleans up the related child versions and the configuration map (Preset Mapping), preventing junk data at the lowest level. In addition, the Domain Models include a real-time conversion algorithm that automatically parses dry Byte data into standard GB/MB formats for the UI.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_2LowLevelInstallation">2. Low-level Installation Execution Flow (Deployment Service)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_TheOrchestrationModuleDeploy">The orchestration module (DeploymentViewModel) works independently from the file-handling logic. Before any batch installation cycle, the system launches a hidden PowerShell with the highest privileges (</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ToCallTheFunction" xml:space="preserve">) to call the function </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ThroughTheWindowsAPI" xml:space="preserve"> through the Windows API. This safeguard ensures the operating system always has a way back if an installer causes conflicts.

</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ForPortableSoftware">For Portable software:</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_TheSystemUses" xml:space="preserve"> The system uses </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ToExtractDirectlyInto" xml:space="preserve"> to extract directly into the target folder (for example C:\\PortableApps), then recursively scans for the main (.exe) file and pushes a PowerShell script that automatically creates a Shortcut on the Desktop.

</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ForSilentInstallers">For Silent Installers:</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ToSolveTheProblem" xml:space="preserve"> To solve the problem of the interface 'freezing' because the installation process does not return stream data, </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_UsesAPollingLoop" xml:space="preserve"> uses a polling loop algorithm (</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ItContinuouslyFeedsRandom">). It continuously feeds random simulated values (</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ToSlowlyPushThe">) to slowly push the Progress Bar up to 95% and anchors it there while waiting for the process to finish. This is an extremely refined UX trick that keeps the software running smoothly.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_3PackageStructureAnalysis">3. Package Structure Analysis Engine (Static Analyzer)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_TheCore" xml:space="preserve">The core </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_WorksAsAStatic" xml:space="preserve"> works as a static binary scanner (Static Binary Scanner). Instead of loading the whole installer into RAM and overflowing memory, the system creates a Stream Buffer strictly limited to </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_TheFirst2MBOf">the first 2MB of data (2048 * 1024 bytes)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ThisBinaryBlockIs" xml:space="preserve">. This binary block is decoded into ASCII encoding to look for the compiler Signatures.

Thanks to this mechanism, SRM automatically distinguishes Inno Setup installers (</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_NullsoftNSISInstallers">), Nullsoft/NSIS installers (</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_OrWiXToolset">), or WiX Toolset (</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_InUnder01" xml:space="preserve">) in under 0.1 seconds, and then precisely injects the </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_DriveRoutingVariablesWithout" xml:space="preserve"> drive-routing variables without any need for user intervention.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_4OpenArchitectureDependency">4. Open Architecture &amp; Dependency Injection (Plugin Ecosystem)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_BuiltOnAModern" xml:space="preserve">Built on a modern Dependency Injection (DI) foundation, all auxiliary features (such as Check RAM, Disk Health) are not crammed into the main core. Instead, they are isolated through the protocol </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_ExternalDLLsOnlyNeed" xml:space="preserve">. External DLLs only need to implement this interface to declare </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_SoTheUICan" xml:space="preserve"> so the UI can automatically render a card. In particular, through the function </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_SRMPassesAllInternal">, SRM passes all internal Services (Database, Logging) back into the Plugins, allowing them to interact deeply with system hardware like a native module.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_Date">Date:</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="About_OpenLogFolder">Open Log folder</system:String>

    <!-- Màn hình: UpdateCenterGuide -->
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_UpdateCenterGuide">Update Center guide</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_UpdateCenterUserGuide">Update Center user guide</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_ThisPageHelpsYou">This page helps you check whether the software in your library has a newer version, and automatically download/install it.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_1ThreeTypesOf">1. Three types of update check sources</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_WingetRecommendedFirst">Winget (recommended first)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_UsesTheReadyMade">Uses the ready-made community catalog of Windows Package Manager. You only need the exact 'package ID' (e.g. VideoLAN.VLC), no need to look up links yourself. Covers most popular software. Requires Winget installed and an internet connection while scanning.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_ForOpenSourceSoftware">For open-source software with a GitHub repo (VLC, Notepad++, OBS...). Just enter 'owner/repo'. The app calls the GitHub API itself to get the latest version + download link.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_WebPageScanRegex">Web page scan + Regex</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_ALastResortWhen">A last resort when the two methods above are unavailable (software of unknown origin, not on Winget). You need to write your own regex to extract the version number from the download page's HTML — fragile when the page changes its layout, use only when really necessary.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_2AutoConfigureNo">2. Auto-configure, no need to set up each app by hand</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_3RowActionButtons">3. Row action buttons</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_ConfigureTheUpdateCheck">Configure the update check source for this software only.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_ScanThisSoftwareRight">Scan this software right now (no need to wait for a scan of the whole library).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_4FilteringAndGrouping">4. Filtering and grouping the list</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_UseTheChipsAll">Use the chips 'All / New version available / Configured / Not configured' to filter quickly. Turn 'Group by category' on or off to group software by Category, which is easier to read when the library has many apps.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_5NotesWhenUsing">5. Notes when using a portable USB drive</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_TheAppItselfDoes">The app itself does not need the internet to run. You only need the internet at the moment you click 'Scan' or 'Download/Install'. If the computer with the USB drive has no internet or no Winget, these actions will report a clear error instead of hanging — you can skip them and do it later on another computer.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_GotIt">Got it</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_The" xml:space="preserve">The </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_AutoConfigure">"Auto-configure"</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_ButtonOnTheToolbar" xml:space="preserve"> button on the toolbar scans the names of all unconfigured software, matches them against a built-in suggestion list (VLC, Chrome, Zalo, Notepad++, Discord...) and saves the configuration for every matching app — no need to open a dialog for each one. Apps that are not in the suggestion list still need to be configured by hand via the ⚙ icon.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_Download">Download:</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_DownloadsTheNewVersion" xml:space="preserve"> downloads the new version and </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_AddsItToThe">adds it to the library</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_DataFolderDBWITHOUT" xml:space="preserve"> (Data/ folder + DB), WITHOUT touching the computer running the app.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_InstallNow">Install now:</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_DownloadsTheNewVersion2" xml:space="preserve"> downloads the new version, adds it to the library, then </system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_InstallsItOnThis">installs it on this computer right away</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UpdateCenterGuide_WithAWingetSource">. With a Winget source, the install step uses the Winget command directly (it cannot be added to the Data/ library, because Winget manages its own cache).</system:String>

